{
  "abstract": "We prove algebraicity of the Weil classes on every polarized abelian sixfold of $\\mathbf Q(i)$-Weil type with signature $(3,3)$ and signed discriminant class $3$ modulo norms. At the full special unitary Hodge group, this proves the rational Hodge conjecture for every power, including very general periods in this nine-dimensional domain. The source construction refines the cyclic determinant correspondence of OpenAI, Lemma 3.4: the Fermat degree can be a common multiple of the inertia orders, independently of the covering degree. Brauer induction extends this refinement to arbitrary finite groups. Classical Fermat results provide further source degrees. At inertia exponent eight or twelve, the source Jacobian is a product of CM elliptic curves, so known elliptic Hodge algebraicity suffices. We apply exponent twelve to $G=\\langle W(E_8),iI_8\\rangle$. An exact character-transform calculation gives total ninth Hurwitz–Hodge intersection $3009825/64$. Every component, including disconnected covers, yields the same sixfold Hermitian datum. Canonical-extension positivity therefore gives a dominant component, and specialization and isogenies reach all periods. A separate six-loop certificate proves full $\\mathrm{SU}(3,3)$ monodromy on the explicit tuple component, without identifying it as the dominant component. The supplement contains exact verifiers and public input data. A bounded-inertia, large-genus whole-Jacobian corollary follows from existing joint monodromy. The results retain the cited geometric cyclic input but do not use a global CM Hodge theorem or the withdrawn split-eightfold preprint. Other discriminant classes and additional special-fibre Hodge classes remain open here.",
